-- Affine wrappers whose inner is NOT a session-kind protocol.
--
-- The wrapper requires its inner to be kind 1S; these inners are *T
-- (proper unrestricted), functions, or compositions with a non-session
-- operand, so the kind check must REJECT. No kind annotation.
--
-- Drive with: AffineKindingInvalidSpec (errorsAreSuccesses).
--
-- Note: unrestricted shared channels (`*!Int : *C`, `*?Int : *C`) ARE
-- accepted as the inner of an affine wrapper because of subkinding
-- (`*C <: 1S`: `Un <: Lin` holds via the polymorphic Mult subsort rule
-- `_ <: Lin{} = True`, and `Channel <: Session` holds via PK subsort).
-- So such cases are NOT placed here.

case **!Int

case **?Float

case **?(Int, Char)

case **!((Int -> Char); Close)

case **!(Int -> Char)

case **!(Skip; Int)

case **?(Skip; Float)

